NAME
    Mojolicious::Command::skapa - Scaffolding commands for Mojolicious
    applications

SYNOPSIS
    # Install
    cpanm Mojolicious::Command::skapa

    # Use from any Mojolicious application
    ./script/myapp skapa <subcommand> [args]

    # Or from the "mojo" command itself
    mojo skapa <subcommand> [args]

DESCRIPTION
    skapa (Old Norse: "to create, to shape") adds Artisan-style code
    generation to Mojolicious. Every subcommand creates files inside the
    current application, resolves paths from the running app's home
    directory, refuses to overwrite existing files, and prints what to
    do next (e.g. which "plugin '...';" line to add to startup).

    The command lives in the shared Mojolicious::Command namespace, so
    it is discovered automatically by Mojolicious::Commands from @INC.
    No configuration, no namespace registration.

SUBCOMMANDS
    make:controller <Name>
        Creates lib/<App>/Controller/<Name>.pm, a Mojolicious::Controller
        subclass with a commented example action. Nested paths
        (Admin/Reports) become nested packages
        (<App>::Controller::Admin::Reports).

    make:plugin <Name>
        Creates lib/<App>/Plugin/<Name>.pm, a Mojolicious::Plugin
        subclass with an empty register method. Prints the
        "plugin '<Name>';" line to add to startup.

    make:helper <Name>
        Same file location as make:plugin, but register installs a
        working $app->helper(<name> => sub { ... }) stub. Helper name
        is derived from <Name> (Greeting -> greeting,
        UserLogin -> user_login).

    make:middleware <Name>
        Creates lib/<App>/Middleware/<Name>.pm. The generated plugin
        supports both route-scoped (returns an $app->routes->under(...)
        subtree for a single route file) and global
        ({ global => 1 } installs an around_action hook) modes. The
        header comment explains both.

    make:route <Name>
        Creates lib/<App>/Route/<Name>.pm, a plugin whose register adds
        routes to $app->routes. Prints the "plugin 'Route::<Name>';"
        line to add to startup.

    make:moo <Name>
        Creates a plain Moo class at lib/<App>/<Name>.pm with
        "use Moo; use strictures 2; use namespace::clean;". Useful for
        service objects, value classes, and non-Mojolicious domain
        classes.

    make:command <name>
        Creates lib/<App>/Command/<name>.pm, a Mojolicious::Command
        subclass with a run method. Prints the
        "push @{$self->commands->namespaces}, '<App>::Command';" line
        to add to startup.

    make:test <name>
        Creates t/<name>.t with a Test::Mojo skeleton (get_ok('/') +
        status_is(200) + done_testing). Name is decamelized
        (UserLogin -> t/user_login.t).

    make:minion <Name>
        Creates lib/<App>/Minion/<Name>.pm, a Minion task class with
        a method stub matching the file name. Prints the
        "use ... ; $self->minion->add_task(<task> => '<package>');"
        lines to add where Minion is started.

    make:request <Name>
        Creates lib/<App>/Requests/<Name>.pm, a
        Mojolicious::Plugin::FormRequest class. Only the "rules"
        method is generated (with a commented example inside).
        Requires Mojolicious::Plugin::FormRequest loaded in startup.

    make:translatable [locale]
        Creates i18n/<locale>.json (default: en) with a starter key.
        Validates the locale format (en, de, pt-BR). Refuses to
        overwrite an existing translation file. Requires
        Mojolicious::Plugin::Translatable loaded in startup.

    make:policy <Name>
        Creates lib/<App>/Policy/<Name>.pm, a plain class (Moo -base,
        not a plugin) with four deny-by-default methods: view, create,
        update, delete. Prints the
        "plugin 'Policy' => { policies => { <Name> => '<package>' } };"
        snippet to add to startup.

    make:secret
        Generates a cryptographically secure secret with
        Mojo::Util::generate_secret and writes it to the app's config
        file (derived from decamelize(ref $app), e.g. Skapa ->
        skapa.yml). If the file already has a top-level "secrets:" key,
        the block is replaced. If no config file exists, prints the
        YAML block for manual copy-paste.

    orm <args...>
        Forwards to the Mimir ORM command if Mimir is loaded
        (migrate, rollback, reset, refresh, fresh, status,
        make:migration, make:model). Prints "Mimir is not loaded" with
        the "plugin 'Mimir';" hint otherwise. Running "skapa orm" with
        no args (or --help) prints a skapa-flavored summary of the
        available ORM commands.

    serve [-l URL] [-x CMD]
        Shortcut for "morbo script/<moniker>". Passes extra args
        straight to morbo, so -l http://*:4000 changes the port and
        -x 'npx vite build --watch' starts an asset bundler in watch
        mode. On a busy port, prints the listen-address hint.

CONVENTIONS
    Every generator follows the same rules:

    - File path is derived from the running app's class
      (ref $self->app) and its home directory, so the command works
      correctly regardless of where the app lives on disk.
    - Existing files are never overwritten. The command prints
      "File already exists: <path>" and exits cleanly.
    - Nothing is auto-edited in lib/<App>.pm (startup). Generators
      print the exact line(s) the user must paste themselves.
    - All generated packages use the app's namespace
      (<App>::Controller::..., <App>::Model::..., etc.), not a
      hardcoded name.

INSTALLATION
    From CPAN (once released):

        cpanm Mojolicious::Command::skapa

    From source:

        git clone https://github.com/<you>/Mojolicious-Command-skapa.git
        cd Mojolicious-Command-skapa
        perl Makefile.PL
        make
        make install

    Verification:

        perl -MMojolicious::Command::skapa -e 'print "loaded\n"'
        mojo skapa

    The command should appear in the "mojo" command list and print
    its usage block when called without a subcommand.

DEPENDENCIES
    Required:
        Mojolicious 9.0+
        Moo 2.0+

    Optional (only if you use the matching subcommand):
        Moo + strictures + namespace::clean  (make:moo)
        Mojolicious::Plugin::FormRequest     (make:request)
        Mojolicious::Plugin::Translatable    (make:translatable)
        Mojolicious::Plugin::Policy          (make:policy)
        Mimir                                 (orm)
        Minion                                (make:minion)

    None of the optional plugins are auto-loaded by this distribution.
    They are used only when the matching generator is invoked; the
    generated code requires them, but the CLI itself does not.

TESTING
    The distribution ships no tests of its own beyond a load check.
    Run the generated code's own tests with "prove -l t/" from the
    target application.

    To verify the install without installing globally:

        cpanm --local-lib=/tmp/skapa-install .
        PERL5LIB=/tmp/skapa-install/lib/perl5 perl \
          -MMojolicious::Command::skapa -e 'print "loaded\n"'

